+## 4. Fresh read-only Supabase evidence
+
+Project `legal`, ref `qqfzbecwhewswkyxgebu`, region `eu-west-1`, PostgreSQL `17.11.0.003`. The environment classification is not exposed by project metadata; treat it as **unclassified and not authorized for writes**. Project, Auth, DB, REST, Storage, pooler and pgBouncer health report active/healthy. Realtime also reports `ACTIVE_HEALTHY` but its detail says `db_connected=false` and `replication_connected=false`; record that operational inconsistency and investigate with the owner before relying on Realtime.
+
+- Supabase migration history lists only `20261022174110 initial_legal_schema_and_rls` and `20261022174313 transactional_rpc_functions`. Neither local candidate migration is applied.
+- Public catalog counts: 18 base tables, 153 columns, 83 constraints, 67 indexes, 54 policies. RLS is enabled on all 18 public tables; `FORCE ROW LEVEL SECURITY` is enabled on none. `anon` and `authenticated` have `rolbypassrls=false`; `service_role` has `rolbypassrls=true` (not superuser).
+- `anon`, `authenticated`, and `service_role` each have all seven table privileges—`SELECT`, `INSERT`, `UPDATE`, `DELETE`, `TRUNCATE`, `REFERENCES`, `TRIGGER`—on all 18 public tables. RLS does not filter `TRUNCATE`, `REFERENCES`, or `TRIGGER`. A direct `TRUNCATE` request through ordinary PostgREST was not attempted and is not claimed; the unsafe grants are confirmed, while direct REST exploitability of those non-DML privileges is not demonstrated.
+- Current column ACLs permit anon/authenticated to select `reviews.user_id` and `lawyers.user_id`, and include broad column privileges on `users` fields such as `email`, `role`, `uid`, and `auth_user_id`. The `users` row policy restricts visible rows, but its UPDATE `WITH CHECK` compares `role`/`email` and does not explicitly compare the `uid`/`auth_user_id` mapping; this is a potential identity-mapping mutation path that needs a real authenticated PostgREST negative test. No such write was attempted.
+- `public.public_reviews` is absent. The raw `reviews` SELECT policy is public, so `reviews.user_id` is directly selectable under the public policy. The candidate safe view is local only.
+- Live public functions: nine; all observed owner `postgres`, `SECURITY DEFINER`, `search_path=public`. The six RLS/trigger helpers (`current_app_user_id`, `current_app_user_role`, `is_admin`, `is_lawyer_or_admin`, `link_migrated_auth_user`, `set_updated_at`) have EXECUTE available to PUBLIC/anon/authenticated/service_role. Three baseline RPCs (`rpc_recalculate_lawyer_rating`, `rpc_reserve_booking_slots`, `rpc_wallet_mutate`) are executable by postgres/service_role, not anon/authenticated. Existing `current_app_user_id()` falls back to `auth.uid()::text` if no application profile is linked. `link_migrated_auth_user()` links by case-insensitive email while `auth_user_id IS NULL`, without a confirmed-email or explicit legacy-ID check. Its trigger is `AFTER INSERT ON auth.users` only. These live definitions remain unchanged.
+- Current FKs without a valid non-partial leading B-tree index: `booking_slots.user_id` (`booking_slots_user_id_fkey`), `lawyers.user_id` (`lawyers_user_id_fkey`), and `subscriptions.plan_id` (`subscriptions_plan_id_fkey`). The hardening candidate adds none of these indexes.
