+# Proposed identity, owner, and lawyer-access hardening
+
+**Status: proposal only.** The SQL and rollback files in this directory are not in `supabase/migrations/`, have not been executed, and require explicit approval before any hosted use. All Supabase queries in this review were read-only.
+
+## Live facts checked on 2026-10-24
+
+- The live schema accepts `client`, `lawyer`, and `admin`; it does not accept `owner`.
+- `private.current_app_user_id()` currently falls back to `auth.uid()::text` when there is no matching `public.users` profile. That means “no profile” is not a fully closed identity boundary for RLS policies that compare a row's `user_id` to this helper.
+- `public.link_migrated_auth_user()` is an `AFTER INSERT ON auth.users` trigger. Its live body links the first unlinked `public.users` row with a case-insensitive matching email. It does not require an explicit legacy profile ID or a confirmed email. Auth configuration currently requires email confirmation before normal sign-in, but email equality is still being used as the legacy identity link. This contradicts the migration documentation and the stated “email alone is not proof” requirement.
+- `users_update_self_or_admin` plus the identity guard allows the current administrator role to change role fields. The role-change RPC referenced by Express is not among the three live `rpc_*` functions, so the current API role-change path is not deploy-verified. This proposal keeps legacy `admin` intact and explicitly reserves `owner` changes for `postgres`/`service_role`.
+- The live `cases` and `bookings` SELECT policies expose owner/admin rows only; they do not grant a lawyer access to rows assigned through `lawyers.user_id`.
+- `public.lawyers.user_id` has a SELECT grant to `anon` and `authenticated`. The existing backend sanitizes its public projection, but direct PostgREST column selection is not similarly hidden. Revoking the authenticated grant is deliberately not bundled here because current admin API queries use that column; it needs a separate compatibility design.
+- No case-history, hearing, or case-document table exists. `bookings` is the existing appointment record; `cases.due_date` is text. No additional tables are proposed here.
+
+## Proposed SQL and expected effect
+
+The exact forward SQL is [`20261024_identity_owner_lawyer_access.sql`](20261024_identity_owner_lawyer_access.sql). It is a reviewed draft, not a migration to apply blindly.
+
+1. **Fail closed on missing/unsupported profile.** Replace the private user ID/role helpers so they return no application identity unless a matching profile has a currently supported role. This removes the live Auth-UUID fallback. Result: RLS owner predicates resolve to false for a missing or invalid profile.
+2. **Stop email-only legacy linking and fix public signup roles.** Replace the Auth trigger so it waits for confirmed email or phone; links a legacy row only when admin-controlled `raw_app_meta_data.legacy_uid` and `legacy_migration_verified=true` identify the exact row and a confirmed email matches. A confirmed phone signup can create a `client` profile only. Normal public email signup also defaults to `client`; only the server-side lawyer-onboarding flow may set `raw_app_meta_data.signup_role='lawyer'` before email confirmation. `raw_user_meta_data.role` is ignored. No client metadata or public flow can create `admin` or `owner`.
+3. **Add `owner` without rewriting existing admins.** Add `owner` to the role check and enforce at most one owner with a partial unique index. Keep every existing `admin` profile; do not rename or bulk-convert accounts. `is_admin()` treats both `admin` and `owner` as privileged. Owner creation/removal, identity remapping, and deletion are reserved for a service-role request with a `service_role` JWT claim or a direct SQL-operator session with no PostgREST JWT. The identity guard does not broadly trust `current_user='postgres'` (which SECURITY DEFINER RPCs also observe); the trusted Auth-link trigger uses a transaction-local marker plus nested-trigger checks for its exact legacy-link update. Ordinary authenticated users, including admins and other SECURITY DEFINER RPCs, cannot alter the owner identity.
+4. **Scope case, booking, and slot policies.** Restrict the existing client-owner policies on `cases`, `bookings`, and `booking_slots` to the `client` role; `admin`/`owner` remains explicitly privileged. Add read-only SELECT access for a lawyer only to cases/bookings assigned through the existing `lawyers.user_id -> users.id` relation. Do not grant lawyer writes or booking-slot reads; existing admin-only booking and slot writes remain unchanged.
+5. **No DML/backfill in the migration.** No existing application rows are intentionally changed. New Auth profiles are created only after the corresponding email/phone confirmation; phone-only signups are fixed to `client`. Existing rows remain linked or unlinked as-is.
+
+### Local verification (isolated PGlite only)
+
+The proposal was applied after all ten active local migrations in an in-memory PGlite database. Synthetic fixtures exercised explicit Auth-UUID mapping precedence (including a conflicting UUID-shaped profile), missing-profile fail-closed helpers, unconfirmed/confirmed email and phone signup, client-only phone signup, ignored caller role metadata, trusted lawyer metadata, exact verified legacy linking, rejection of email-only linking, client-owned case reads/writes, assigned-lawyer case/booking reads, no lawyer writes or booking-slot reads, owner-only provisioning, rejection of owner creation/demotion through authenticated and SECURITY DEFINER paths, the single-owner index, and the companion rollback. The RLS fixture mirrored only the relevant local table grants. `node --test test/supabase_migrations.test.js` passes 16/16; targeted route/Auth tests pass 90/90; full backend `npm test` passes 513/513 across 123 suites. These are local fixtures/PGlite tests only—not hosted PostgreSQL 17, Supabase Auth/PostgREST, or production E2E verification. Flutter/Dart are unavailable in this workspace, so Admin Panel and mobile Flutter tests were not run.
+
+### Rollback
+
+The exact reverse SQL is [`20261024_identity_owner_lawyer_access_rollback.sql`](20261024_identity_owner_lawyer_access_rollback.sql). It aborts before changing anything if an `owner` row exists, then restores the helper/Auth-trigger/identity-guard definitions observed live, removes the added lawyer policies and owner-protection triggers/functions, drops the single-owner index, and restores the original role constraint.
+
+**Security caveat:** executing that rollback restores the email-only Auth trigger and Auth-UUID fallback that this proposal is intended to remove. It is technically reversible, but not a recommended operational rollback after public signup has resumed. Prefer a forward corrective migration. If a rollback is approved, first disable the affected signup paths and establish how to preserve accounts created after the forward migration. No rollback has been run.
+
+## Owner provisioning runbook (draft; not performed and currently blocked)
+
+**Deployment blocker:** local source now recognizes the server-verified `owner` role, routes it through admin authorization, accepts a server-provisioned `lawyer` session into a read-only panel workspace, and includes a public lawyer-signup endpoint gated off by default. These changes are not deployed; the live database still rejects `owner`, the live project has no isolated test branch, Flutter tests were not runnable in this workspace, and the endpoint's redirect allow-list is not configured. Do not provision an owner, enable lawyer signup, or change hosted Auth/RLS until the reviewed SQL and corresponding backend/panel builds are separately approved, deployed, and verified.
+
+1. First obtain approval for the role/trigger migration and complete a recoverable backup/restore test. Apply only the reviewed migration in a controlled window.
+2. Create a dedicated Auth user using the authorized Supabase Auth Admin/Invite flow. The intended mailbox owner confirms the address. Do not use a client-side role field or user metadata.
+3. Obtain the Auth UUID from the trusted Auth Admin interface. Match the profile by `public.users.auth_user_id = <that UUID>`; do not match or authorize by email alone. Stop if there is not exactly one row, the address is unconfirmed, or the row is not an ordinary `client` profile created for this new account.
+4. Use a private, one-off operator process with `SUPABASE_URL`, `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY`, and that verified UUID supplied through the process environment. The service key must not enter Flutter, the browser, Git, logs, or chat. The process should assert that no `owner` exists, re-check the exact Auth UUID and confirmed status, update only that profile from `client` to `owner`, and verify the returned row. Do not promote any existing `admin` or `lawyer` row automatically.
+5. Only after an owner-aware backend/Admin release is deployed, verify owner login and RLS behavior with a client JWT and negative tests; record the change in the authorized audit/change log. If either the proposal migration or matching app/backend release is missing or unverified, stop. The live database rejects `owner`; deployed application compatibility has not been verified.
+
+The checked-in SQL files are enough for review; the runbook does not authorize or execute provisioning.
+
+## Gates still required before enabling public signup
+
+- Review and approve the SQL; test it on an isolated PostgreSQL 17/Supabase environment with confirmed and unconfirmed Auth users, an existing unlinked legacy profile, normal client signup, trusted lawyer signup, invalid/missing profiles, and role boundaries.
+- The connected Auth configuration currently has `site_url=http://localhost:3000` and an empty redirect allow-list. Supply the intended web/mobile callback URI and obtain approval before changing production Auth settings.
+- The project currently reports no deployed Edge Functions. The lawyer signup endpoint and AI/document functions are local source only. The lawyer endpoint requires `ENABLE_LAWYER_SIGNUP=true` plus an explicit redirect, defaults closed, and accepts no role/profile IDs from the browser.
+- The mobile client defaults `ENABLE_CLIENT_SIGNUP` to `false`. Do not enable either signup path until the identity migration and callback flow have been approved, applied, and verified.
diff --git a/supabase/proposals/20261024_identity_owner_lawyer_access.sql b/supabase/proposals/20261024_identity_owner_lawyer_access.sql
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..1d0f02e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/supabase/proposals/20261024_identity_owner_lawyer_access.sql
@@ -0,0 +1,432 @@
+-- PROPOSAL ONLY — NOT IN supabase/migrations/ and NOT applied to any project.
+-- Target was inspected read-only on 2026-10-24. Review the companion .md first.
+-- Uses only existing `users`, `lawyers`, `cases`, and `bookings` tables.
+-- No data rows are intentionally changed by this transaction.
+
+BEGIN;
+
+-- A profile is required for application identity. Never fall back to the Auth
+-- UUID when the trusted profile is absent or carries an unsupported role.
+CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION private.current_app_user_id()
+RETURNS text
+LANGUAGE sql
+STABLE
+SECURITY DEFINER
+SET search_path = pg_catalog, public
+AS $function$
+  WITH matched_profile AS (
+    SELECT u.id, u.role
+    FROM public.users AS u
+    WHERE auth.uid() IS NOT NULL
+      AND (u.auth_user_id = auth.uid() OR u.id = auth.uid()::text)
+    ORDER BY (u.auth_user_id = auth.uid()) DESC NULLS LAST,
+             (u.id = auth.uid()::text) DESC NULLS LAST
+    LIMIT 1
+  )
+  SELECT id
+  FROM matched_profile
+  WHERE role IN ('client', 'lawyer', 'admin', 'owner');
+$function$;
+
+CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION private.current_app_user_role()
+RETURNS text
+LANGUAGE sql
+STABLE
+SECURITY DEFINER
+SET search_path = pg_catalog, public
+AS $function$
+  WITH matched_profile AS (
+    SELECT u.role
+    FROM public.users AS u
+    WHERE auth.uid() IS NOT NULL
+      AND (u.auth_user_id = auth.uid() OR u.id = auth.uid()::text)
+    ORDER BY (u.auth_user_id = auth.uid()) DESC NULLS LAST,
+             (u.id = auth.uid()::text) DESC NULLS LAST
+    LIMIT 1
+  )
+  SELECT role
+  FROM matched_profile
+  WHERE role IN ('client', 'lawyer', 'admin', 'owner');
+$function$;
+
+-- `admin` remains a compatibility role. It is not renamed or converted.
+-- New `owner` profiles receive the same DB authorization used by existing
+-- owner/admin policies; the partial unique index below allows at most one.
+ALTER TABLE public.users DROP CONSTRAINT users_role_check;
+ALTER TABLE public.users
+  ADD CONSTRAINT users_role_check
+  CHECK (role IN ('client', 'lawyer', 'admin', 'owner')) NOT VALID;
+ALTER TABLE public.users VALIDATE CONSTRAINT users_role_check;
+
+CREATE UNIQUE INDEX users_single_owner_key
+  ON public.users (role)
+  WHERE role = 'owner';
+
+CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION private.is_admin()
+RETURNS boolean
+LANGUAGE sql
+STABLE
+SECURITY DEFINER
+SET search_path = pg_catalog, public
+AS $function$
+  SELECT COALESCE(
+    private.current_app_user_role() IN ('admin', 'owner'),
+    false
+  );
+$function$;
+
+CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION private.is_lawyer_or_admin()
+RETURNS boolean
+LANGUAGE sql
+STABLE
+SECURITY DEFINER
+SET search_path = pg_catalog, public
+AS $function$
+  SELECT COALESCE(
+    private.current_app_user_role() IN ('lawyer', 'admin', 'owner'),
+    false
+  );
+$function$;
+
+-- Keep existing admin role changes for client/lawyer accounts compatible, but
+-- reserve both promotion to and demotion from owner for a trusted SQL/service
+-- role. Ordinary authenticated clients cannot set identity or role columns.
+CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION public.guard_user_identity_fields()
+RETURNS trigger
+LANGUAGE plpgsql
+SET search_path = pg_catalog, public
+AS $function$
+BEGIN
+  IF (OLD.role = 'owner' OR NEW.role = 'owner') AND (
+    NEW.id IS DISTINCT FROM OLD.id
+    OR NEW.uid IS DISTINCT FROM OLD.uid
+    OR NEW.auth_user_id IS DISTINCT FROM OLD.auth_user_id
+    OR NEW.role IS DISTINCT FROM OLD.role
+  ) THEN
+    -- SECURITY DEFINER RPCs run with current_user set to their function owner
+    -- (often postgres). That alone is not operator authority: distinguish a
+    -- service-role JWT from authenticated callers, and allow direct SQL
+    -- operator sessions only when no PostgREST JWT role is present.
+    IF (current_user = 'service_role' AND auth.role() = 'service_role')
+       OR (session_user = 'postgres' AND auth.role() IS NULL) THEN
+      RETURN NEW;
+    END IF;
+    RAISE EXCEPTION 'The owner identity and role can only be changed by a trusted provisioning process'
+      USING ERRCODE = '42501';
+  END IF;
+
+  IF (
+    NEW.id IS DISTINCT FROM OLD.id
+    OR NEW.uid IS DISTINCT FROM OLD.uid
+    OR NEW.auth_user_id IS DISTINCT FROM OLD.auth_user_id
+    OR NEW.role IS DISTINCT FROM OLD.role
+  ) AND NOT COALESCE(
+    current_setting('legal.auth_user_link_in_progress', true) = 'true'
+    AND current_user = 'postgres'
+    AND pg_trigger_depth() > 1,
+    false
+  ) AND NOT public.is_admin() THEN
+    RAISE EXCEPTION 'Identity and role fields can only be changed by an administrator'
+      USING ERRCODE = '42501';
+  END IF;
+  RETURN NEW;
+END;
+$function$;
+
+-- The live users INSERT policy permits authenticated admins to create users,
+-- so reserve owner creation itself for the trusted provisioning path.
+CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION public.guard_owner_profile_insert()
+RETURNS trigger
+LANGUAGE plpgsql
+SECURITY INVOKER
+SET search_path = pg_catalog, public
+AS $function$
+BEGIN
+  IF NEW.role = 'owner'
+     AND NOT COALESCE(
+       (current_user = 'service_role' AND auth.role() = 'service_role')
+       OR (session_user = 'postgres' AND auth.role() IS NULL),
+       false
+     ) THEN
+    RAISE EXCEPTION 'The owner profile can only be created by a trusted provisioning process'
+      USING ERRCODE = '42501';
+  END IF;
+  RETURN NEW;
+END;
+$function$;
+REVOKE ALL ON FUNCTION public.guard_owner_profile_insert() FROM PUBLIC, anon, authenticated;
+DROP TRIGGER IF EXISTS guard_owner_profile_insert_trigger ON public.users;
+CREATE TRIGGER guard_owner_profile_insert_trigger
+  BEFORE INSERT ON public.users
+  FOR EACH ROW
+  EXECUTE FUNCTION public.guard_owner_profile_insert();
+
+-- RLS permits administrators to delete users, so reserve deletion of the
+-- singleton owner account for the same trusted operator path as provisioning.
+CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION public.guard_owner_profile_delete()
+RETURNS trigger
+LANGUAGE plpgsql
+SECURITY INVOKER
+SET search_path = pg_catalog, public
+AS $function$
+BEGIN
+  IF OLD.role = 'owner'
+     AND NOT COALESCE(
+       (current_user = 'service_role' AND auth.role() = 'service_role')
+       OR (session_user = 'postgres' AND auth.role() IS NULL),
+       false
+     ) THEN
+    RAISE EXCEPTION 'The owner profile can only be deleted by a trusted provisioning process'
+      USING ERRCODE = '42501';
+  END IF;
+  RETURN OLD;
+END;
+$function$;
+REVOKE ALL ON FUNCTION public.guard_owner_profile_delete() FROM PUBLIC, anon, authenticated;
+DROP TRIGGER IF EXISTS guard_owner_profile_delete_trigger ON public.users;
+CREATE TRIGGER guard_owner_profile_delete_trigger
+  BEFORE DELETE ON public.users
+  FOR EACH ROW
+  EXECUTE FUNCTION public.guard_owner_profile_delete();
+
+-- Do not claim a legacy profile on email equality. Legacy linking requires an
+-- exact profile ID in admin-controlled raw_app_meta_data plus a confirmed,
+-- matching email. Email and phone signups create profiles only after the
+-- corresponding contact is confirmed. Only a trusted server-controlled
+-- signup_role can request a lawyer profile; raw_user_meta_data.role is ignored.
+-- Phone-only signups are always clients, and all other values (including
+-- admin/owner) fail closed to client.
+CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION public.link_migrated_auth_user()
+RETURNS trigger
+LANGUAGE plpgsql
+SECURITY DEFINER
+SET search_path = pg_catalog, public
+AS $function$
+DECLARE
+  v_legacy_uid text;
+  v_name text;
+  v_signup_role text;
+  v_email_confirmed boolean;
+  v_phone_confirmed boolean;
+BEGIN
+  v_email_confirmed := NEW.email IS NOT NULL AND NEW.email_confirmed_at IS NOT NULL;
+  v_phone_confirmed := NEW.phone IS NOT NULL AND NEW.phone_confirmed_at IS NOT NULL;
+  IF NOT v_email_confirmed AND NOT v_phone_confirmed THEN
+    RETURN NEW;
+  END IF;
+
+  -- Do not treat an unconfirmed address/number change as a verified identity.
+  -- A simultaneous confirmation of the other contact may still provision a
+  -- client profile, but only already-confirmed contact values are persisted.
+  IF TG_OP = 'UPDATE'
+     AND OLD.email IS DISTINCT FROM NEW.email
+     AND OLD.email_confirmed_at IS NOT DISTINCT FROM NEW.email_confirmed_at
+     AND OLD.phone_confirmed_at IS NOT DISTINCT FROM NEW.phone_confirmed_at THEN
+    RETURN NEW;
+  END IF;
+  IF TG_OP = 'UPDATE'
+     AND OLD.phone IS DISTINCT FROM NEW.phone
+     AND OLD.phone_confirmed_at IS NOT DISTINCT FROM NEW.phone_confirmed_at
+     AND OLD.email_confirmed_at IS NOT DISTINCT FROM NEW.email_confirmed_at THEN
+    RETURN NEW;
+  END IF;
+
+  -- Keep an existing explicit Auth mapping; update only confirmed contacts,
+  -- never the stored application role or identity columns.
+  UPDATE public.users
+     SET email = CASE WHEN v_email_confirmed THEN NEW.email ELSE email END,
+         phone = CASE WHEN v_phone_confirmed THEN NEW.phone ELSE phone END,
+         updated_at = now()
+   WHERE auth_user_id = NEW.id;
+  IF FOUND THEN
+    RETURN NEW;
+  END IF;
+
+  -- Legacy rows require both an administrator-verified exact ID and a
+  -- confirmed, matching email. Phone alone is never used to claim legacy data.
+  v_legacy_uid := NULLIF(btrim(NEW.raw_app_meta_data ->> 'legacy_uid'), '');
+  IF v_email_confirmed
+     AND v_legacy_uid IS NOT NULL
+     AND NEW.raw_app_meta_data ->> 'legacy_migration_verified' = 'true' THEN
+    -- The row's existing identity guard only permits identity updates from an
+    -- admin. Mark this exact, nested Auth trigger update rather than broadly
+    -- trusting current_user=postgres (which SECURITY DEFINER RPCs also use).
+    PERFORM set_config('legal.auth_user_link_in_progress', 'true', true);
+    UPDATE public.users
+       SET auth_user_id = NEW.id,
+           email = NEW.email,
+           updated_at = now()
+     WHERE id = v_legacy_uid
+       AND auth_user_id IS NULL
+       AND lower(email) = lower(NEW.email);
+    PERFORM set_config('legal.auth_user_link_in_progress', 'false', true);
+    -- A failed explicit mapping is left unlinked for manual reconciliation.
+    RETURN NEW;
+  END IF;
+
+  v_name := btrim(COALESCE(NEW.raw_user_meta_data ->> 'name', ''));
+  IF char_length(v_name) < 2 THEN
+    v_name := CASE
+      WHEN v_email_confirmed THEN split_part(NEW.email, '@', 1)
+      ELSE 'Client'
+    END;
+  END IF;
+  IF char_length(btrim(v_name)) < 2 THEN
+    v_name := 'Client';
+  END IF;
+
+  -- Lawyer onboarding is an email-confirmed flow assigned by the trusted
+  -- server. A verified phone signup can create a client profile only.
+  v_signup_role := CASE
+    WHEN v_email_confirmed
+     AND NEW.raw_app_meta_data ->> 'signup_role' = 'lawyer' THEN 'lawyer'
+    ELSE 'client'
+  END;
+
+  INSERT INTO public.users (id, uid, auth_user_id, name, email, phone, role)
+  VALUES (
+    NEW.id::text,
+    NEW.id::text,
+    NEW.id,
+    v_name,
+    CASE WHEN v_email_confirmed THEN NEW.email ELSE '' END,
+    CASE WHEN v_phone_confirmed THEN NEW.phone ELSE '' END,
+    v_signup_role
+  )
+  ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
+
+  RETURN NEW;
+END;
+$function$;
+
+DROP TRIGGER IF EXISTS trg_auth_users_link_migrated ON auth.users;
+CREATE TRIGGER trg_auth_users_link_migrated
+  AFTER INSERT OR UPDATE OF email, email_confirmed_at, phone, phone_confirmed_at ON auth.users
+  FOR EACH ROW
+  EXECUTE FUNCTION public.link_migrated_auth_user();
+
+REVOKE ALL ON FUNCTION private.current_app_user_id() FROM PUBLIC, anon;
+REVOKE ALL ON FUNCTION private.current_app_user_role() FROM PUBLIC, anon;
+REVOKE ALL ON FUNCTION private.is_admin() FROM PUBLIC, anon;
+REVOKE ALL ON FUNCTION private.is_lawyer_or_admin() FROM PUBLIC, anon;
+GRANT EXECUTE ON FUNCTION private.current_app_user_id() TO authenticated, service_role;
+GRANT EXECUTE ON FUNCTION private.current_app_user_role() TO authenticated, service_role;
+GRANT EXECUTE ON FUNCTION private.is_admin() TO authenticated, service_role;
+GRANT EXECUTE ON FUNCTION private.is_lawyer_or_admin() TO authenticated, service_role;
+REVOKE ALL ON FUNCTION public.link_migrated_auth_user() FROM PUBLIC, anon, authenticated;
+
+-- Owner policies must be role-bound before any assigned-lawyer policy is
+-- added. A profile with a matching user_id is a client owner only when its
+-- server-owned role is `client`; admin/owner access remains explicit.
+DROP POLICY IF EXISTS cases_select_owner_or_admin ON public.cases;
+CREATE POLICY cases_select_owner_or_admin ON public.cases
+  FOR SELECT TO authenticated
+  USING (
+    private.is_admin()
+    OR (
+      private.current_app_user_role() = 'client'
+      AND user_id = private.current_app_user_id()
+    )
+  );
+
+DROP POLICY IF EXISTS cases_insert_owner_or_admin ON public.cases;
+CREATE POLICY cases_insert_owner_or_admin ON public.cases
+  FOR INSERT TO authenticated
+  WITH CHECK (
+    private.is_admin()
+    OR (
+      private.current_app_user_role() = 'client'
+      AND user_id = private.current_app_user_id()
+    )
+  );
+
+DROP POLICY IF EXISTS cases_update_owner_or_admin ON public.cases;
+CREATE POLICY cases_update_owner_or_admin ON public.cases
+  FOR UPDATE TO authenticated
+  USING (
+    private.is_admin()
+    OR (
+      private.current_app_user_role() = 'client'
+      AND user_id = private.current_app_user_id()
+    )
+  )
+  WITH CHECK (
+    private.is_admin()
+    OR (
+      private.current_app_user_role() = 'client'
+      AND user_id = private.current_app_user_id()
+    )
+  );
+
+DROP POLICY IF EXISTS cases_delete_owner_or_admin ON public.cases;
+CREATE POLICY cases_delete_owner_or_admin ON public.cases
+  FOR DELETE TO authenticated
+  USING (
+    private.is_admin()
+    OR (
+      private.current_app_user_role() = 'client'
+      AND user_id = private.current_app_user_id()
+    )
+  );
+
+DROP POLICY IF EXISTS bookings_select_owner_or_admin ON public.bookings;
+CREATE POLICY bookings_select_owner_or_admin ON public.bookings
+  FOR SELECT TO authenticated
+  USING (
+    private.is_admin()
+    OR (
+      private.current_app_user_role() = 'client'
+      AND user_id = private.current_app_user_id()
+    )
+  );
+
+-- `bookings_write_admin_only` and `booking_slots_write_admin_only` remain
+-- unchanged, including their server/admin-only writes. Booking-slot rows
+-- contain booking/user identifiers and are deliberately not exposed to lawyers.
+DROP POLICY IF EXISTS booking_slots_select_owner_or_admin ON public.booking_slots;
+CREATE POLICY booking_slots_select_owner_or_admin ON public.booking_slots
+  FOR SELECT TO authenticated
+  USING (
+    private.is_admin()
+    OR (
+      private.current_app_user_role() = 'client'
+      AND user_id = private.current_app_user_id()
+    )
+  );
+
+-- Lawyer access is restricted to read-only assigned cases/bookings. The
+-- relationship is `lawyers.user_id -> public.users.id`, not Auth UUID equality.
+CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION private.is_current_user_lawyer_for(p_lawyer_id text)
+RETURNS boolean
+LANGUAGE sql
+STABLE
+SECURITY DEFINER
+SET search_path = pg_catalog, public
+AS $function$
+  SELECT COALESCE(
+    auth.uid() IS NOT NULL
+    AND p_lawyer_id IS NOT NULL
+    AND private.current_app_user_role() = 'lawyer'
+    AND EXISTS (
+      SELECT 1
+      FROM public.lawyers AS l
+      WHERE l.id = p_lawyer_id
+        AND l.user_id = private.current_app_user_id()
+    ),
+    false
+  );
+$function$;
+REVOKE ALL ON FUNCTION private.is_current_user_lawyer_for(text) FROM PUBLIC, anon;
+GRANT EXECUTE ON FUNCTION private.is_current_user_lawyer_for(text) TO authenticated, service_role;
+
+DROP POLICY IF EXISTS cases_select_assigned_lawyer ON public.cases;
+CREATE POLICY cases_select_assigned_lawyer ON public.cases
+  FOR SELECT TO authenticated
+  USING (private.is_current_user_lawyer_for(lawyer_id));
+
+DROP POLICY IF EXISTS bookings_select_assigned_lawyer ON public.bookings;
+CREATE POLICY bookings_select_assigned_lawyer ON public.bookings
+  FOR SELECT TO authenticated
+  USING (private.is_current_user_lawyer_for(lawyer_id));
+
+COMMIT;
